![Changes (days/year) in predicted dates of first egg hatch for SUNP across the CONUS over the entire 44-year period (1981–2025). Maps show (A) all changes and (B) statistically significant changes (P < 0.1); areas shown in gray are not statistically significant.](./SUNP/figure2.png){#fig-sunp-egg-hatch fig-align='center' width=70%}
:::
:::


#### **Recent period: 2001--2025**

During 2001–2025, earlier predicted phenology remained evident across much of the West and central United States, while later events occurred in portions of the northern and eastern interior (@fig-sunp-emergence-recent, @fig-sunp-egg-hatch-recent). Significant changes were spatially limited.


